## Why This Is Asked
Tests SwiftUI, Combine, and simple disk persistence in a beginner-friendly way, plus lifecycle handling.

## Key Concepts
- SwiftUI state management and data binding
- Combine debounce to throttle rapid changes
- Lightweight persistence to disk (Documents) with Codable or plain text
- Lifecycle considerations (background/foreground)

## Code Example
```swift
import SwiftUI
import Combine

class NoteViewModel: ObservableObject {
  @Published var text: String = ""
  @Published var wordCount: Int = 0

  private var cancellables = Set<AnyCancellable>()

  init() {
    $text
      .debounce(for: .milliseconds(300), scheduler: RunLoop.main)
      .map { $0.split(whereSeparator: { $0 == " " || $0 == "\n" }).count }
      .assign(to: \.wordCount, on: self)
      .store(in: &cancellables)
  }

  func saveToDisk() {
    // write to Documents/notes.txt
  }
}
```

